@!internal

module nupp.runtime.services.catalog

--[[
Static declarations for compiler-carried runtime implementations.

Entries name a service identity, API version, canonical contract module and
handle export, provider module/member, and compatible dialect. The compiler uses
these records with dependency capability metadata to check exports, form artifact
closures, invalidate caches, and support implementation navigation. Reading this
module never executes a provider body.

The facade map identifies consumers that require service-backed operations.
Runtime initialization uses an artifact's compatible catalog when present and
the compiler-carried catalog otherwise. Catalog ordering never chooses a default;
facade assembly or explicit setup makes that decision.

Third-party packages publish capability descriptors as described in
[Service Providers](docs/learn/projects/service-providers.md). They do not edit or
import this internal catalog as a registration API.
]]

--- Compiler-carried provider declarations. Entries contain no implementation code.
